flowchart TB
  accTitle: OpenTask task delivery lifecycle
  accDescr: A draft passes creation approval, awaits acceptance, is accepted and started by its owner, and has its result accepted or returned by the reviewer. Checklist completion does not complete the task.
  draft["Draft · creator only"] -->|Creator submits for approval| approval["Creation approval"]
  approval -->|Approver returns| returned["Returned for editing"]
  returned -->|Creator edits and resubmits| approval
  approval -->|Team leader gives final approval| pending["Awaiting acceptance · team-visible"]
  draft -.->|Team leader creates and issues directly| pending
  pending -->|Owner accepts task| accepted["Accepted"]
  accepted -->|Owner starts work| working["In progress"]
  pending -->|Owner accepts and starts| working
  working -->|Owner submits result<br/>Current agreement must be confirmed| review["Awaiting review"]
  review -->|Reviewer returns result<br/>Gaps and next feedback time required| working
  review -->|Reviewer accepts result<br/>Prerequisites must be complete| done["Completed · cannot reopen"]
  classDef active fill:#EDF3F8,stroke:#365FAC,color:#28344B,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef terminal fill:#DCE7FA,stroke:#365FAC,color:#28344B,stroke-width:2px;
  class draft,approval,returned,pending,accepted,working,review active;
  class done terminal;
